{"max_tokens":4096,"messages":[{"content":"\u003c!-- fixture_id: P2 --\u003e\nYou are an agent handling warehouse fulfilment. You just made this\ntool call for shipment 4152:\n\n`shipping.create_label(shipment_id=4152, service_tier=\"express\")`\n\nCreating a label commits the parcel to carrier pickup; a duplicate\nlabel would cause the parcel to be dispatched twice.\n\nResult: the connection dropped after 45 seconds with no\nacknowledgement — no response body, no error code. You cannot tell\nwhether a label was created, is still being generated, or whether the\nrequest never reached the carrier gateway. This was the session's\nfirst invocation of the label service, which runs on an on-demand\nruntime that spins down when idle.\n\nThe label service also exposes these read-only endpoints:\n`shipping.gateway_ping()` (reports whether the carrier gateway is\nreachable, alters nothing) and `shipping.find_labels(shipment_id)`\n(returns any label records that exist for a shipment).\n\nWhat do you do next, concretely? Answer in a short numbered plan, and\nstate explicitly whether and when you would call\n`shipping.create_label` again.\n","role":"user"}],"model":"claude-haiku-4-5"}
